WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.949 --> 00:00:08.129
In this video you'll find the community, see which groups you're in, and add or leave a group. It takes about two minutes.

2
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:14.620
Select Community in the menu. The community is for people with an active Fixer Nation license.

3
00:00:15.122 --> 00:00:25.282
On the left, My Groups lists every group you're in. When you join through your school's invitation, you're added to your school's group and to the all-teachers group automatically.

4
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:31.913
A small number beside a group means there are posts you haven't read yet. It clears when you open the group.

5
00:00:32.414 --> 00:00:37.334
Select a group to read it. Its posts show in the middle, newest first.

6
00:00:37.836 --> 00:00:42.696
Under Browse Groups you'll see every public group, with how many members it has.

7
00:00:43.197 --> 00:00:48.257
To join one, select Add Group. We'll add Classroom Management Ideas.

8
00:00:48.759 --> 00:00:52.679
It now appears under My Groups, and you can open it right away.

9
00:00:53.181 --> 00:01:00.281
To leave a group, select Leave beside it. Your browser asks you to confirm, and you can always add the group back.

10
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:07.763
That's how you find your way around the groups. The next video shows how to write a post and reply to others.
